Emit the atomic counter of an append or consume structured buffer on the C++ target.

lowerAppendConsumeStructuredBuffers (source/slang/slang-ir-lower-append-consume-structured-buffer.cpp)
turns an AppendStructuredBuffer or ConsumeStructuredBuffer into an element buffer and a counter of
Atomic<int>, and its Append and Consume into an AtomicInc or AtomicDec of the counter. The C++
emitter (source/slang/slang-emit-cpp.cpp) emits AtomicAdd through the prelude's
_slang_atomic_add_* helpers and has no case for AtomicInc or AtomicDec, which therefore reach the
default and are reported as E99999 "unimplemented feature in Slang compiler: unexpected IR opcode
during code emit". The SPIR-V, DXIL and HLSL targets compile the same shader.

This emits AtomicInc and AtomicDec as an add of 1 and of -1 through the same helpers, which return
the prior value, as the HLSL emitter's InterlockedAdd does for the two. A regression test is added
as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-cpp-append-consume-buffer.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 (win-x64): E99999 for a compute shader with an append and a consume buffer on
the C++ target.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-emit-cpp.cpp b/source/slang/slang-emit-cpp.cpp
index 2974d07..3bba444 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-emit-cpp.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-emit-cpp.cpp
@@ -1365,7 +1365,15 @@ bool CPPSourceEmitter::tryEmitInstStmtImpl(IRInst* inst)
             return true;
         }
     case kIROp_AtomicAdd:
-        {
+    case kIROp_AtomicInc:
+    case kIROp_AtomicDec:
+        {
+            // AtomicInc and AtomicDec are an add of 1 and of -1 through the same helpers, and like
+            // them return the prior value, as HLSL's InterlockedAdd does for these two. They are the
+            // counter of an AppendStructuredBuffer or ConsumeStructuredBuffer, which
+            // lowerAppendConsumeStructuredBuffers (slang-ir-lower-append-consume-structured-buffer.cpp)
+            // turns into an atomic increment or decrement of an Atomic<int>.
+            //
             // Lower AtomicAdd on a pointer-to-uint/int slot to a call
             // through the CPU prelude helpers. Matches HLSL/GLSL
             // semantics: returns the prior value as the inst result.
@@ -1415,7 +1423,12 @@ bool CPPSourceEmitter::tryEmitInstStmtImpl(IRInst* inst)
             // chosen by `emitOperand` from the IR operand's type, so
             // the literal width here matches the chosen `helper`
             // signature automatically.
-            emitOperand(inst->getOperand(1), getInfo(EmitOp::General));
+            if (inst->getOp() == kIROp_AtomicInc)
+                m_writer->emit("1");
+            else if (inst->getOp() == kIROp_AtomicDec)
+                m_writer->emit("-1");
+            else
+                emitOperand(inst->getOperand(1), getInfo(EmitOp::General));
             // Operand 2 (memory order) is consumed by the prelude
             // helpers in `slang-cpp-prelude.h`, not threaded through
             // here; see those helpers for the per-toolchain ordering
